Short:        ANSI BBS terminal: telnet/rlogin/modem
Author:       NilBBS
Uploader:     NilBBS
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      1.5.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.0+, 68020+, a TCP/IP stack or a modem
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

NilTerm calls BBSes the way SyncTERM does on a PC.

 - Its own 640x400 16-colour screen (graphics card or High Res Laced) with
   80 columns of the IBM VGA 8x16 font and the PC's colours; full ANSI
   (cursor movement, colours, scroll regions, insert/delete), CP437.
 - Telnet done properly: terminal type ANSI, window size, binary mode, and
   the cursor-position answers BBSes use to detect ANSI.
 - Telnet, rlogin, raw TCP, or a modem / direct line on the serial port.
 - A dialing directory: per system its connection, address or phone number,
   user name + password with auto-login (or Alt+L), screen, line speed,
   iCE colours and download folder; call counts and last-call dates;
   quick connect to any host:port.
 - An Amiga screen mode for Amiga BBSes: Topaz from ROM, Latin-1, 0x9B CSI.
 - Modem-speed emulation (300-115200 bps, Alt+Up/Down) for ANSI animations;
   iCE colours (bright backgrounds) and blinking text.
 - A status bar with the system and time online; Alt-key hotkeys.
 - ZMODEM downloads that start by themselves; ZMODEM, YMODEM and XMODEM(-1K)
   upload and download; progress on the status bar, Esc cancels.
 - 2000 lines of scrollback, session capture (raw ANSI or plain text),
   copy the screen to the clipboard and paste into a call.
 - Settings for the download / upload / capture folders and the modem.

Install with the included Installer script, or copy the NilTerm drawer
anywhere.  The manual is NilTerm.guide.  Use the .lha: a .zip can't carry
the AmigaDOS protection bits (then: Protect NilTerm/NilTerm +e).

NilTerm is part of NilBBS, a telnet BBS for AmigaOS.  MIT licence.

The screen font is IBM VGA 8x16 from "The Ultimate Oldschool PC Font Pack"
by VileR, https://int10h.org/oldschool-pc-fonts/ - CC BY-SA 4.0.
